  "question": {
    "text": "A particle, of mass <math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;kg</mi></math> and charge <math><mn>1.0</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>C</mn></math>, is initially at rest. At time <math><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, the particle comes under the influence of an electric field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>E</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>t</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>&#160;</mi><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> where <math><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn><mi>&#160;N</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mn>C</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math><mi>&#969;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;rad</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mn>s</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Consider the effect of only the electrical force on the particle. Then the maximum speed, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>m</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mn>s</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>, attained by the particle at subsequent times is ____________.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;kg</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1&#160;</mn><mn>C</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Force on particle will be<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />At <math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> <math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><msub> <mi>t</mi> <mi>o</mi> </msub> <mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow> </mrow></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></math><br /><math><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">sin</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>d</mn><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>d</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>v</mi></msubsup><mn>d</mn><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#8725;</mo><mi>&#969;</mi></mrow></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mr